 dressup.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Xiamen/Xiamen Island"},{"id":"xiamen_wv_yuanxiangkou_fish_balls","areaId":"xiamen","name":"Yuanxiangkou Fish Balls","category":"food","tags":["food"],"location":{"lat":24.45106,"lng":118.06271},"visitMinutes":75,"photoSeed":"xiamen_wv_yuanxiangkou_fish_balls","tickets":[{"vendor":"Official","url":"http://www.yxkyw.com","official":true}],"signals":{},"hashtags":["yuanxiangkoufishballs","xiamen"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"}],"note":"Typical hours — check the official site"},"summary":"An award-winning shop that is most famous for its fish balls, which are stuffed with pork and cooked in a savory soup. Try the fish balls alone (¥6) or with noodles (¥8). Unless you're an adventurous foodie and/or read Chinese well enough to understand exactly what you're getting, however, skip the other \"snacks\" (小吃) even though they're supposed to be famous Gulangyu specialties.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Xiamen/Gulangyu"},{"id":"xiamen_wv_me_you_2","areaId":"xiamen","name":"Me & You 2","category":"food","tags":["food"],"location":{"lat":24.4772,"lng":118.0714},"visitMinutes":75,"photoSeed":"xiamen_wv_me_you_2","tickets":[],"signals":{},"hashtags":["meyou2","xiamen"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"}],"note":"Typical hours — check the official site"},"summary":"Owner is a cheerful Scandinavian; decor includes some Viking-themed items. Good menu with both Asian and Western options including a large range of pizzas from ¥45-65 (they also deliver). They have Becks, Tiger and 